- op: discuss  # 23d7
  at: '2026-03-20T09:25:15Z'  # 23d7
  by: agent  # 23d7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 23d7
  clock: 2  # 23d7
  nonce: 23d7  # 23d7
  message: "minisign and git-crypt use C stdlib IO functions (fopen, fread, fwrite, fgets, fprintf) as direct function calls, but the C analyzer does not create call edges for them. The IO primitive catalog has these functions listed but there are no call edges to match against. This means C repos get 0 IO boundary matches for file operations. Discovered in security-claims bakeoff Cohort 1 (git-crypt: 0 fs_read/fs_write chains) and Cohort 2 (minisign: 0 total IO edges). The C++ alias fix helped git-crypt pick up 4 subprocess edges (execvp/wait) but no fs operations."  # 23d7
